<rml>
<head>
<title>Wyświetlacz peronowy</title>
<!--
Example (TSRE displays): a platform screen; the clock beside it is a
document of its own (zegar.rml).

Shapes: wyswietlacz_zegar_wiszacy_1.sd, _2.sd and
wyswietlacz_peron_zegar_wiszacy.sd: squares (700 x 500, Surface Glass,
RefreshRate 5, Input Platform) over the screen's part of each face's
LCD, zegar.rml's over the clock's part, the screen on the same end on both
faces (the end over the platform's edge). The platform's screens share
one document, drawn every 5 seconds; the clocks share one for the route,
drawn every second. A redraw costs a millisecond or more of the CPU (the
Steam Deck, 2026-11-03), so what changes every second is kept small.

Shows:
- the platform's next train (display.trains' first: the platform's trains,
  each once, in the order they come): leaving, its departure and
  destination (the train's own, else its last stop's station); ending
  here, its arrival and origin; the platform, the train (its fields, else
  its timetable name);
- when it leaves or arrives: in how many minutes, by TSRE's functions
  add_minutes (the booked time plus the delay) and minutes_until (from the
  clock, display.clock); a late train's delay and its expected time;
- its cars from the front (row.cars: the platform's next two trains have
  them): a box a vehicle with its number, the loco with a rounded nose,
  the colour by its tags (has): first class yellow, second light,
  restaurant red, sleeping and couchette blue; over 10 vehicles in two
  rows of 10, past 20 left out.

Data binding and TSRE's functions; no Lua.
-->
<style>
body, div {
    display: block;
}
span {
    display: inline;
}
body {
    margin: 0;
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
    background-color: #050608;
    color: #ffffff;
    font-family: Noto Sans;
}

/* The next departure. */
#panel {
    position: absolute;
    left: 27px;
    top: 7%;
    width: 646px;
    height: 86%;
    padding: 18px 22px;
    box-sizing: border-box;
    background-color: #0d2b8c;
}
.head {
    font-size: 56px;
    font-weight: bold;
}
.time {
    margin-right: 22px;
}
.label {
    margin-top: 12px;
    color: #c3cff5;
    font-size: 18px;
}
.value {
    font-size: 30px;
}
.late {
    color: #ffcc33;
}
.train {
    position: absolute;
    left: 22px;
    bottom: 16px;
    font-size: 30px;
    font-weight: bold;
}
.operator {
    margin-right: 10px;
    color: #c3cff5;
    font-size: 22px;
}

/* The next train's cars from its front: a box a vehicle, its number on
   it. An engine dark, its nose rounded at the train's front or rear; the
   colour by the tags after that (an EMU's power car carries passengers).
   Up to 10 sharing the row; more in two rows of 10 (from the 21st on
   left out), the strip growing upwards. */
.cars {
    position: absolute;
    left: 22px;
    right: 22px;
    bottom: 66px;
    height: 44px;
    display: flex;
}
.cars.two {
    height: 80px;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
}
.cars.two .car {
    flex: none;
    width: 55px;
    height: 36px;
    margin-bottom: 4px;
    line-height: 36px;
    font-size: 20px;
}
.car {
    flex: 1;
    margin-right: 4px;
    height: 44px;
    line-height: 44px;
    background-color: #9aa3b5;
    color: #0d1424;
    font-size: 24px;
    font-weight: bold;
    text-align: center;
}
.car.loco {
    background-color: #2a303c;
    color: #ffffff;
}
.car.front {
    border-radius: 20px 0 0 20px;
}
.car.back {
    border-radius: 0 20px 20px 0;
}
.car.first {
    background-color: #f2c200;
    color: #0d1424;
}
.car.second {
    background-color: #eef1f6;
    color: #0d1424;
}
.car.restaurant {
    background-color: #d83a34;
    color: #ffffff;
}
.car.sleeping {
    background-color: #3a6ee8;
    color: #ffffff;
}

</style>
</head>
<body data-model="display">

<div id="panel">
    <div data-for="row, i : trains">
        <div data-if="i == 0">
            <!-- Leaving: its departure and where it goes; ending here: its
                 arrival and where it comes from. -->
            <div class="head" data-if="row.departs != ''">
                <span class="time">{{row.departs}}</span>
                <span>{{row.destination}}</span>
            </div>
            <div class="head" data-if="row.departs == ''">
                <span class="time">{{row.arrives}}</span>
                <span>{{row.origin}}</span>
            </div>

            <div class="label">Peron / Platform</div>
            <div class="value">{{platform}}</div>

            <div data-if="row.departs != ''">
                <div class="label">Odjazd / Departure</div>
                <div class="value" data-if="(row.departs | add_minutes(row.delay) | minutes_until(clock)) > 0">
                    za {{row.departs | add_minutes(row.delay) | minutes_until(clock)}} min
                </div>
                <div class="value" data-if="(row.departs | add_minutes(row.delay) | minutes_until(clock)) &lt;= 0">
                    odjeżdża / departing
                </div>
            </div>
            <div data-if="row.departs == ''">
                <div class="label">Przyjazd / Arrival</div>
                <div class="value" data-if="(row.arrives | add_minutes(row.delay) | minutes_until(clock)) > 0">
                    za {{row.arrives | add_minutes(row.delay) | minutes_until(clock)}} min
                </div>
                <div class="value" data-if="(row.arrives | add_minutes(row.delay) | minutes_until(clock)) &lt;= 0">
                    przyjeżdża / arriving
                </div>
            </div>
            <div class="value late" data-if="row.delay != ''">
                opóźnienie {{row.delay}} min, ok. {{row.time | add_minutes(row.delay)}}
            </div>

            <!-- Its cars from the front. -->
            <div class="cars" data-class-two="row.cars.size &gt; 10">
                <div class="car" data-for="v : row.cars" data-if="v.index &lt; 20"
                     data-class-loco="v.kind == 'engine'"
                     data-class-front="v.kind == 'engine' &amp;&amp; v.index == 0"
                     data-class-back="v.kind == 'engine' &amp;&amp; v.index &gt; 0 &amp;&amp; v.index == row.cars.size - 1"
                     data-class-first="v.tags | has('A')"
                     data-class-second="v.tags | has('B')"
                     data-class-restaurant="v.tags | has('WR')"
                     data-class-sleeping="(v.tags | has('WL')) || (v.tags | has('BC'))">{{v.number}}</div>
            </div>

            <!-- The train's fields where it has them, else its timetable name. -->
            <div class="train" data-if="row.operator != '' || row.category != '' || row.line != ''">
                <span class="operator">{{row.operator}}</span>
                {{row.category}} {{row.number}} {{row.line}} {{row.name}}
            </div>
            <div class="train" data-if="row.operator == '' &amp;&amp; row.category == '' &amp;&amp; row.line == ''">
                {{row.id}}
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>

</body>
</rml>
